Package: liblsl2
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Lab Streaming Layer core library (runtime)
 The Lab Streaming Layer (LSL) is a system for unified collection of
 measurement time series in research experiments. It handles networking,
 time-synchronisation, (near-)real-time access and centralised collection
 and recording of data over a local network. LSL is widely used to acquire
 and synchronise data from EEG, eye tracking, motion capture, audio and
 many other sources in neuroscience and psychophysiology experiments.
 .
 This package provides the shared library (liblsl.so.2) used at runtime by
 applications and language bindings built against LSL.

Package: liblsl-dev
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libdevel
Depends:
 liblsl2 (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Lab Streaming Layer core library (development files)
 The Lab Streaming Layer (LSL) is a system for unified collection of
 measurement time series in research experiments. It handles networking,
 time-synchronisation, (near-)real-time access and centralised collection
 and recording of data over a local network.
 .
 This package provides the C and C++ headers and the CMake package
 configuration (the LSL::lsl imported target) needed to build applications
 and language bindings against the LSL core library.
